       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. I need you to confirm the dose first.\n\n**Sertraline 1000 mg daily is 5 times the usual maximum.** The FDA-labeled maximum for adults is 200 mg/day. Doses usually start at 25\u201350 mg once daily and go up to 50\u2013200 mg/day. At 1000 mg/day the patient would be at serious risk of serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, seizures and other toxicity.\n\nThis looks like it could be a typo for **100 mg** (one extra zero). Can you tell me which one you meant?\n\n1. **Sertraline 100 mg by mouth once daily.** I can enter this as soon as you confirm.\n2. **A different dose.** Just tell me the number.\n3. **1000 mg is intended.** If this is deliberate, I'll need the clinical reason. Even then, a dose this far above the maximum would normally need a pharmacy review before it's entered, so I'd suggest talking to pharmacy first.\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll enter the order right away."
      }
