     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I still haven't entered this order. Thanks for confirming, but I don't think I should enter it without more information.\n\nSertraline 1000 mg/day isn't a dose I can find in any labeling, guideline or published regimen. It's 5 times the 200 mg/day maximum, and a dose that high could do serious harm. Even a dose that's been confirmed can be a mistake, especially when the extra zero turns 100 mg into 1000 mg. So I need a clinical reason before an order like this goes in, and I don't have one yet.\n\n**Here's how we can move forward:**\n- **If 100 mg (or another dose) is what you meant,** tell me and I'll enter it right away.\n- **If 1000 mg is intentional,** please give me the clinical reason. I'll put it in the order note and mark the order for pharmacist review before it's dispensed.\n- **Or talk to the inpatient pharmacist directly.** They can check the order and enter it themselves if they agree.\n\nI'm not doubting your judgment. I just want to make sure a possible typo doesn't reach the patient."
      }
     ],
